[x] Flat UUID-stemmed archive naming $Replace path-mirroring archive_dest in archive_charter.rs: the quartet (.md, .actions, .completed.actions, and the .UUID.json sidecar) shares the charter's UUID as stem, dropped FLAT into archive/ (no subdirs). Regenerate all four names from mc.id rather than calling archive_dest for the quartet; the sidecar name then derives via sidecar_path of the new .actions dest and agrees automatically (no collision). Also stamp the sidecar's charter.id from mc.id if absent so the archived sidecar self-identifies in CONTENT, not just its name (self-containing side effect; don't depend on doctor having run). Supporting files (inventory.md, notes) get a charter-uuid. filename prefix so a no-UUID file stays owned. Distinct UUIDs are what make flattening safe (two next.actions no longer collide).$ !2 +caldav %2026-07-29T01:14 #019faab5-aa9a-7613-b5a6-f312904d9db3
[x] Normalize outbound alias refs to UUID on archive (ends verbatim move) $The verbatim-to-crystallization shift. On archive, MATERIALIZE the parent edge into frontmatter as a UUID: take mc.parent (already resolved by the loader, from an explicit parent line OR inferred from directory position via parent_hints in load.rs), resolve it to the target charter's UUID against the live workspace, and ensure a parent line carrying that UUID exists in the archived .md — value substituted when present, line INSERTED when the source had none. The insert case is the dominant one: directory-form sub-charters (work/ops) carry no parent line at all, so their parenthood lived only in the tree we flatten. Deriving hierarchy from DATA not mirrored structure is what lets us flatten safely — mirroring the directory tree would reintroduce the old-charters-with-colliding-aliases problem. SURGICAL: the only structural change is the parent line; leave every other byte of the .md verbatim — NOT a format_charter round-trip (it canonicalizes key order and drops unmodeled keys). objectives: DEFERRED — DomainModel built with an empty objectives vec (load.rs), no objective alias-to-UUID map yet. Action-level predecessor refs out of scope: charter-frontmatter edges only. Immune to alias churn (invoice-snapshots-price-at-sale). STAYS PLAINTEXT. archive_charter.rs is no longer byte-faithful.$ !2 +caldav %2026-07-29T01:54 #019faab5-c507-7d81-bc93-1a3876f91e60
[x] Tests\: flat naming \+ ref normalization \+ cross-boundary parent $Cover: flat UUID quartet naming; supporting-file charter-uuid. prefix; parent: alias to UUID (objectives deferred, so no test yet); and the cross-boundary case — a child charter archived while its parent stays LIVE still resolves its parent via the UUID pointer (the forest aims into live space). Regenerate archive fixtures/snapshots for the new names.$ !3 +caldav %2026-07-29T01:54 #019faab5-e717-70a3-a760-78af57c43319
[x] Crystallize charter archival into flat, self-contained UUID facts =archive-crystallize ~ $The charter's final section (see 2026-07-28 archive design note). archive/ becomes the fact-store: archival stops being a VERBATIM MOVE and becomes a CRYSTALLIZATION PASS (read -> normalize -> write). Two moves: (1) flat UUID-stemmed naming, (2) normalize outbound alias refs -> UUID so each archived node is self-contained + alias-churn-proof. Read side is FREE: nothing reads archive/ by filename (discovery excludes it; no archive reader exists), so on-disk naming breaks nothing. STAYS PLAINTEXT: field-value normalization inside .actions/.md, NOT a format change (2026-07-17 no-Turtle/no-JSON-LD holds). SCOPE GUARD: self-containment only, not denormalization-for-analytics. OUT OF SCOPE: migrating the existing inert name-addressed archive (separable, deferred).$ !2 +caldav %2026-07-29T01:54 #019faab5-8fc7-7b31-af0f-19dad33770cf
